# Production Data Cutover (CO-CUTOVER-001)

Status: **ENTERPRISE APPROVED** · Super Administrator only  
Depends on: **CO-ADMIN-004 Production Reset** (engine + wizard)

## Objective

Remove historical **demo / development** transactional data before live production while preserving:

1. All enterprise master / configuration data  
2. All genuine live business records  

## Hard rules

1. **Never delete** Users, Roles, Permissions, Organisation, Products, Product Categories, Lenders, Product-Lender Matrix, Workflow / Rules / Policy engines, Identity Registry, Registry metadata, Lookup / Source masters, Templates, Settings.
2. **Never delete** unmarked live Contacts, Companies, Opportunities, Deals, Tasks, Documents, Notes, Activities, Timelines.
3. Target **demo heuristics only** via preset `demo_data_only` (DEMO/TEST/UAT prefixes, `createdBy=demo-seed`, `.demo` emails, import batches).
4. **Analyse before execute.** No deletion until Super Admin reviews the Cutover Validation Report.
5. Feature flag **default OFF** (`PRODUCTION_RESET_ENABLED`).
6. After cleanup, **rebuild derived metrics** (EME Force Recalculate) from remaining live data only.

## SSOT

| Concern | Path |
|--------|------|
| Engine | `server/services/production-reset/` |
| Demo filters | `server/services/production-reset/filters.ts` |
| Cutover analyse API | `GET /api/admin/production-reset?view=cutover` |
| Wizard | `/admin/production-reset` |
| Validation report | `docs/co-cutover-001/CO-CUTOVER-001-PRODUCTION-DATA-CUTOVER-VALIDATION-REPORT.md` |

## Forbidden

- Truncating the database  
- Using `production_cutover` preset when live transactions must be retained  
- Auto-delete on deploy or implementation  
- Inventing a second reset engine outside Production Reset
